Subject: [PATCH 0/2] Fold org-style headings in long mail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:17:29 +0000

Long agent replies are hard to navigate in notmuch-show, which only
collapses whole messages. This series gives a message's sections the
expand and collapse of org-mode, without running org-mode on mail.

Patch 1 makes each org-style heading in a text/plain part a button
that folds its section. It uses a regexp and overlays only, the same
way the diff highlighting in pm-notmuch.el works, because list mail is
untrusted and turning on org-mode has run code from the text it was
turned on for.

Patch 2 asks agents to head the sections of long mail that way, since
they use dash-underlined titles today, which do not fold.

Testing: I indexed a two-message thread in a scratch notmuch database
and ran notmuch-show over it in emacs --batch with pm-notmuch loaded.
The reply, shown at depth 1, had "* One", "** One.a" and "* Two" and a
quoted "> * quoted heading". The three headings became buttons with
the outline-1 and outline-2 faces, and the quoted line stayed plain
text. Pushing each button hid exactly its section, and pushing it
again showed it. Folding "* Two", the last section, stopped at the end
of the part. pm-notmuch.el byte-compiles with no new warnings. I have
not tried it in a graphical session.

